p.src:
Four-velocity has four components but only three independent degrees of freedom. Dividing the interval identity by $d\tau^2$ gives $1
=
\left(\frac{dt}{d\tau}\right)^2
-\left(\frac{d\vec x}{d\tau}\right)^2,$ or $\boxed{
(u^0)^2-\vec u^{\,2}=1
}.$ The one normalization condition removes one independent component.

