p.src:
Relativity adds a third demand: every inertial observer must agree on the action. The natural infinitesimal scalar available on a timelike worldline is $d\tau$. Therefore the free-particle action is $\boxed{
S=-m\int_a^b d\tau
}
\qquad(c=1).$ The finite-sum picture is $S=-m\lim_{N\to\infty}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\Delta\tau_k.$ Since every observer agrees on each proper-time increment, every observer agrees on which path makes their sum stationary.

