p.src:
The statement $\sum p^\mu_{\mathrm{initial}}
=
\sum p^\mu_{\mathrm{final}}$ applies to an isolated system containing everything that exchanges energy and momentum. Real laboratories have stray electric and magnetic fields, ambient particles, gravity, supports, and detectors. If one leaves those degrees of freedom outside the bookkeeping, the subsystem can show a small apparent imbalance; the missing four-momentum has gone into the environment.

