p.src:
It is important not to confuse the exact formula with its low-speed expansion: $\begin{aligned}
E_{\mathrm{exact}}
&=
\frac{mc^2}{\sqrt{1-v^2/c^2}},
\\
E_{\mathrm{slow}}
&=
mc^2+\frac12mv^2
+O\!\left(\frac{mv^4}{c^2}\right).
\end{aligned}$ The first remains valid for every $v<c$. The second is useful only when $v/c\ll1$.

